  "aciklama": "Qantas 32 suffered an uncontained engine failure. The cause: misaligned counterbore thinning an oil feed stub pipe, leading to fatigue, oil fire and turbine disc failure.\n\nFailure chain: Pipe bored off-centre → Wall too thin → Fatigue crack leaks oil → Oil fire → Turbine disc bursts\n\nAnother reconstruction: The Disaster That Ended the Age of the Airship — https://youtu.be/PGOKZhPYo7c\n\nFootage & sources:\n• Archival film: \"Qantas Flight 32 damage.png\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Qantas_Flight_32_damage.png\n• Archival film: \"Qantas A380-800 VH-OQC Trent 900 nacelle.jpg\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Qantas_A380-800_VH-OQC_Trent_900_nacelle.jpg\n• Archival film: \"Qantas a380 vh-oqa takeoff heathrow arp.jpg\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Qantas_a380_vh-oqa_takeoff_heathrow_arp.jpg\n• Archival film: \"2 x A380s on final approach (6066307789).jpg\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2_x_A380s_on_final_approach_(6066307789).jpg\n\nTechnical references:\n• Wikipedia — Qantas Flight 32 — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qantas_Flight_32\n• Australian Transport Safety Bureau — ao 2010 089 final (cited by Wikipedia) — http://www.atsb.gov.au/media/4173625/ao-2010-089_final.pdf\n\nNarration uses a synthetic voice. Footage is real archival film or licensed stock; anything reconstructed is labelled on screen.\n\nFailure File · Episode 21 · A new engineering failure, reconstructed every day.\n\n#shorts #engineering #Qantas32 #materials #history",
